<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=telegraph">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Communication and computing</p><h1 class="enc-title">Telegraph</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The telegraph was a system for transmitting messages over long distances by electrical signals along wires, developed in the nineteenth century. Submarine cables linked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and other parts of its empire, greatly accelerating imperial communication and commerce. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> count the telegraph among the technologies through which the empire integrated a global network.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/telegraph.jpg" alt="Telegraph" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PSM_V09_D091_Morse_key_and_register.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1816</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>London</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Francis Ronalds · <a href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Georges-Louis Le Sage had an electric telegraph working between two rooms in 1774; the first commercial system, Cooke and Wheatstone’s, dates from 1837.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/voltaic-pile">Electric battery<span>1800</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/telephone">Telephone<span>1861</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/radio">Radio<span>1895</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=telegraph">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
